cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenAVMKit in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenAVMKit: an open source toolkit for real estate mass appraisal"
abstract: >-
  OpenAVMKit is a free and open source Python library for real estate mass
  appraisal. It provides modules for data cleaning, spatial data enrichment,
  automated valuation modeling (multiple regression, geographically weighted
  regression, and gradient-boosted trees), and IAAO-standard ratio and equity
  studies, together with Jupyter notebooks that implement a reproducible
  end-to-end assessment pipeline for any jurisdiction.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Doucet
    given-names: Lars A.
repository-code: "https://github.com/larsiusprime/openavmkit"
url: "https://www.openavmkit.com/"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - mass appraisal
  - automated valuation model
  - AVM
  - CAMA
  - property tax
  - property assessment
  - ratio study
  - IAAO
  - real estate
  - GIS
  - Python
version: 0.6.0
date-released: "2026-06-05"
